        difficultyReason = "Thirteen landmarks across two continents.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Thirteen landmarks across two continents.\n\n1. Track Surveying the Damage and inspect its thirteen separate criteria. This is a travel achievement; launch-era comments about automatic login credit are not instructions for a new Retail character.\n\n2. KALIMDOR NORTH: visit the Ruins of Auberdine in Darkshore, Thunder Peak in Ashenvale and Southfury Watershed in Durotar. In Darkshore, use Zidormi's pre-Battle for Azeroth phase if the newer warfront landscape prevents discovery.\n\n3. KALIMDOR SOUTH/WEST: visit the Battlescar in Southern Barrens, Cenarion Wildlands in Desolace, the Shimmering Deep in Thousand Needles, and the Valley of the Watchers in southern Tanaris. Move close enough to each landmark for its zone text/criterion to register.\n\n4. EASTERN KINGDOMS NORTH: visit the Greymane Wall in southern Silverpine, Ruins of Southshore in Hillsbrad and the broken Stonewrought Dam in northern Loch Modan.\n\n5. EASTERN KINGDOMS SOUTH: visit the Scar of the Worldbreaker in Badlands, the Raging Chasm in Westfall, and the Sundering at Northern Stranglethorn's southern waterfall. Check all thirteen criteria before retracing a continent.",
