    [4853] = {
        achievementId = 4853,
        name = "Glory of the Cataclysm Raider",
        category = "Raids",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Glory of the Cataclysm Raider",
        description = "A guaranteed personal reward for twelve Heroic raid bosses and their encounter challenges across three raids. This is separate from the guild's Dark Phoenix unlock.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Multiple raids require deliberate add handling, health thresholds and debuff timing; failed kills consume a weekly lockout.\n\n1. Track Glory of the Cataclysm Raider (4853), inspect its unfinished criteria and set legacy Raid Difficulty to Heroic before entering each raid. You need every listed Heroic boss kill as well as the special challenges below. Unlike Dark Phoenix, this mount does not require a guild group.\n\n2. BLACKWING DESCENT: fly to the high outside balcony on Blackrock Mountain's eastern face, around Burning Steppes 26.1,23.8. Enter the raid portal there; going down the internal chains leads toward different instances.\n\n3. Magmaw - Parasite Evening: kill him before a player becomes infected by a Lava Parasite; if adds spawn, keep them off players. Omnotron - Achieve-a-tron: burst the active construct before Static Shock, Poison Bomb, Arcane Annihilator or Flamethrower can hit anyone. These are quick kills at high level, and both must also give Heroic completion.\n\n4. Maloriak - Aberrant Behavior: aggro without damaging him below his final-phase threshold. Let Release Aberrations finish repeatedly until at least 12 Aberrations are alive; each successful release adds three. Gather them away from the boss and kill 12 within ten seconds, then finish Maloriak. Do not interrupt every release or let a damage aura kill adds as they appear.\n\n5. Atramedes - Silence is Golden: kill him before anyone's sound reaches 50. If the fight lasts, dodge the sound discs and use the room's gongs to reset sound before the limit. Chimaeron - Full of Sound and Fury: defeat him without any raid member dying. A fast high-level kill meets both conditions without recreating the old raid damage cycle.\n\n6. Nefarian - Keeping it in the Family: jump into the pit and keep Onyxia alive while Nefarian arrives. Carefully lower Nefarian below 50% without killing him; roughly 40-45% leaves a clear margin. Kill Onyxia before her energy fills. During the lava phase climb a pillar, kill the Chromatic Prototype there and interrupt dangerous casts. Wait until the lava recedes and Nefarian LANDS for the final phase, then kill him. A premature airborne kill can miss credit.\n\n7. BASTION OF TWILIGHT: fly high above the southwestern Twilight Highlands to the spire's summit portal, around 34.2,78.0. Enter on Heroic. Halfus - The Only Escape: release two available drakes, gather them and kill both within ten seconds of each other, then kill Halfus. Do not kill Halfus before freeing and defeating the drakes.\n\n8. Valiona and Theralion - Double Dragon: hold boss damage and wait for the Twilight Realm entry mechanic. Stand in Theralion's Dazzling Destruction ground effects to enter the realm, then find and kill six Twilight Fiends there. Use /target Twilight Fiend to find them among the purple effects. After the six are credited, leave through a portal if needed and finish the dragons.\n\n9. Ascendant Council - Elementary: reduce the first pair together, then the second pair, without excessive damage. Before Elementium Monstrosity forms, stand near the EDGE of the purple central circle. Keep it stationary and kill it promptly so it creates only one Liquid Ice pool. Standing at the exact center can make it move after spawning and create a second pool; that correction comes from the guide's replies.\n\n10. Cho'gall - The Abyss Will Gaze Back Into You: stay close to him and kill him before any player's Corrupted Blood reaches 30. Dismiss a taunting pet if it would pull him away and expose a solo character to mind control. Finish his Heroic kill; Sinestra beyond him is optional for this mount.\n\n11. THRONE OF THE FOUR WINDS: fly to the airborne platform off southwestern Uldum at 38.4,80.6 and enter on Heroic. The Conclave's three bosses occupy separate outer platforms connected by wind bridges. Do not kill Nezir immediately: this attempt needs Stay Chill first.\n\n12. Conclave - Stay Chill: stand on Nezir's northern platform and let Wind Chill reach at least seven stacks on every player who needs credit. While that condition is active, defeat Nezir and cross the wind bridges to finish Anshal and Rohash before the first boss recovers. A helper covering an outer platform makes the timing easier. Track the condition and kill all three within their recovery window rather than repeatedly waiting for a dead boss to revive.\n\n13. Al'Akir - Four Play: click an outer platform's central wind funnel to reach him. Carefully lower his health to start phase two, then STOP before the final flight transition. Wait for a Stormling. Move it beside Al'Akir and kill it there so the boss receives Feedback; killing it far away gives no debuff. Confirm Feedback on Al'Akir, then burst him down before it expires, including the short flight transition.\n\n14. Check all 24 criteria in 4853. If a setup failed, finish that missing achievement on a suitable eligible character or after the weekly reset. When the meta completes, check the Mount Journal and reward mail for Reins of the Drake of the East Wind and learn it. Completing Guild Glory alone does not award this personal mount.",
        stepCount = 14,
        waypoints = {
            {
