        difficultyReason = "A travel route with no boss or competitive requirement.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A travel route with no boss or competitive requirement.\n\n1. Track Explore Twilight Highlands and use a flying mount. This route includes both factions' settlements for exploration; do not land among hostile guards unnecessarily. The current checklist includes Crucible of Carnage and the Krazzworks, omitted by some older comment lists.\n\n2. Sweep the southern and eastern settlements: Highbank (78, 75); Twilight Shore (71, 71); Obsidian Forest (57, 81); Crushblow (47, 77); The Twilight Citadel (29, 73); Dunwald Ruins (46, 69); Highland Forest (54, 63); Victor's Point (43, 58); Firebeard's Patrol (61, 56); Dragonmaw Port (75, 57); Gorshak War Camp (62, 49); Crucible of Carnage (50, 58). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n3. Cross the western pass and central basin: Grim Batol (24, 56); Wyrms' Bend (29, 48); Dragonmaw Pass (25, 37); Vermillion Redoubt (34, 33); Glopgut's Hollow (36, 35); The Gullet (37, 39); The Twilight Breach (40, 46); Bloodgulch (56, 42); Slithering Cove (70, 41). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n4. Finish the northern loop: Thundermar (47, 28); Humboldt Conflagration (39, 21); Ruins of Drakgor (44, 14); The Maw of Madness (51, 11); Kirthaven (57, 18); The Black Breach (59, 30); The Krazzworks (75, 16). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n5. Reopen the tracked achievement and revisit only unchecked locations. Fly low or land when an overhead pass does not reveal a subzone; the drawn map label alone is not proof of discovery. These are exploration objectives, so you do not have to finish the zone's quest campaign.",
