        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4869#comments",
    },
    [4870] = {
        achievementId = 4870,
        name = "Coming Down the Mountain",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Coming Down the Mountain",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Complete several connected quest chapters, including their prerequisite hand-ins.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete several connected quest chapters, including their prerequisite hand-ins.\n\n1. Enable Trivial Quests on the minimap and track this achievement's CURRENT named chapters. Old comments' numeric quest totals predate storyline tracking. Turn in each branch's final quest and take its follow-up before leaving the hub. Begin at Nordrassil in OUTDOOR Mount Hyjal with Protect the World Tree. Complete the Flameseer's Staff / Baron Geddon, Alysra and prisoner-rescue opening, then Return to Nordrassil.\n\n2. Follow The Return of the Ancients to Goldrinn's shrine. Complete the Lycanthoth confrontation and the shrine's remaining story hand-ins. Goldrinn's branch opens the subsequent ancient work; flying to the later shrines does not skip those prerequisites.\n\n3. Complete the Grove of Aessina and Tortolla branches, following the rescue/firefighting quests and Ysera's appearances. If the route seems to stop after jousting, look for Last Stand at Whistling Grove around 19,40 rather than farming another set of incidental side quests.\n\n4. At the Shrine of Aviana, complete the egg/Sethria storyline and The Hatchery Must Burn. Enter the hatchery portal and finish Farden's jousting introduction through Egg Wave; the current Aviana chapter needs this branch even though an older comment called it optional.\n\n5. Finish Aessina's Miracle and return to the Sanctuary of Malorne. At a 6/9-chapter stall, check the physical quest givers here for Seeds of Their Demise (25491) and Firebreak (25492); later comments report that their follow-ups restore The Ancients chain even when the world map shows no large quest marker.\n\n6. Follow the Twilight-cult infiltration and southern Firelands assault through the Gates of Sothann and the scripted Ragnaros confrontation. Complete Extinguish the Firelord and its hand-in, then check all NINE chapters. Molten Front daily unlocks are a later campaign and do not replace the remaining Hyjal finale.",
