        name = "Explore the Cape of Stranglethorn",
        category = "Exploration",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Explore the Cape of Stranglethorn",
        difficulty = "easy",
        difficultyReason = "A travel route with no boss or competitive requirement.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A travel route with no boss or competitive requirement.\n\n1. Track this achievement and select the map matching each route leg. The Sundering is credited from the Northern Stranglethorn waterfall approach even though it belongs to the Cape checklist. Older unqualified /way 45 70 macros land near Booty Bay when used on the Cape map.\n\n2. Approach the Sundering carefully from the rocks above the northern waterfall; do not fall into the whirlpool: The Sundering - Northern Stranglethorn waterfall approach (50.56, 69.84). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n3. Visit the Cape's northern ruins: Gurubashi Arena (47, 20); Crystalvein Mine (64.39, 29.8); Ruins of Jubuwal (55, 30); Hardwrench Hideaway (38, 39). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n4. Loop around the southern cape: Ruins of Aboraz (60, 47); Mistvale Valley (54, 58); Nek'mani Wellspring (42, 52); Booty Bay (44, 72); Wild Shore (51, 66); Jaguero Isle (56, 73). Approach each location until its exploration criterion is checked.\n\n5. Reopen the tracked achievement and revisit only unchecked locations. Fly low or land when an overhead pass does not reveal a subzone; the drawn map label alone is not proof of discovery. These are exploration objectives, so you do not have to finish the zone's quest campaign.",
