        difficultyReason = "Reach Al'Akir's Stormling phase without overshooting it, then kill him with Feedback active.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Reach Al'Akir's Stormling phase without overshooting it, then kill him with Feedback active.\n\n1. Enter Throne of the Four Winds on Normal or Heroic, defeat the Conclave and use its central wind route to Al'Akir. Disable pets, procs and automatic damage before pulling him.\n\n2. Carefully reduce Al'Akir into phase two, roughly 65-70% in the recent successful guide, then STOP. Do not push him into the final flight phase before a Stormling has spawned. A lower-level helper or damage-reduction toy can be needed even after removing gear.\n\n3. Wait for a Stormling, move it next to Al'Akir and kill the ADD there. Inspect Al'Akir's debuffs and verify Feedback is present; killing the add too far from him does not apply it.\n\n4. Immediately finish Al'Akir before Feedback expires, including the flight transition if it occurs. Do not kill the boss merely because an add died: the debuff must actually be on him. The preferred recent profit comments and their replies emphasize controlling damage rather than using old fixed hit counts.",
