    [5478] = {
        achievementId = 5478,
        name = "The Limnologist",
        category = "Professions",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "The Limnologist",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Forty-two freshwater catches across several continents, including rare school catches.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Forty-two freshwater catches across several continents, including rare school catches.\n\n1. Learn Fishing, track The Limnologist and compare its CURRENT forty-two criteria. Catch and LOOT the required fish yourself; buying fish or receiving them from another player does not grant catch credit. Keep bag space available. The map pins identify fishing shores/search areas, not guaranteed first-cast drops.\n\n2. SOUTHERN EASTERN KINGDOMS: fish Elwynn's inland lakes for Brilliant Smallfish, Stormwind canals for Longjaw Mud Snapper, and Lake Everstill in Redridge for Bristle Whisker Catfish. Fish the Loch in Loch Modan for Loch Frenzy, and cast into Sagefish Schools there for Sagefish.\n\n3. WESTERN PLAGUELANDS: fish inland water around the Darrowmere shore for Mithril Head Trout, and target Greater Sagefish Schools for Greater Sagefish. These are two separate species; an ordinary Sagefish does not fill the Greater Sagefish criterion.\n\n4. DEADWIND PASS: fish the water around Karazhan for Bloodfin Catfish AND Crescent-Tail Skullfish. Remain until both criteria are checked; neither is one of the removed Bloated-fish requirements.\n\n5. KALIMDOR / TIRISFAL: fish the Forgotten Pools in Northern Barrens around 36,46 for Deviate Fish; target its Deviate Fish Schools when available. Fish Tirisfal's inland water for Sickly Looking Fish, selecting the earlier Tirisfal phase with Zidormi if the post-Battle for Azeroth state interferes. For Nightfin Snapper, use the Tainted Forest's inland water in EARLIER Blasted Lands, preferably during evening/night game time; it is time-sensitive, unlike ordinary all-day catches.\n\n6. DEEPHOLM: fish open inland water for Albino Cavefish, Lavascale Catfish and Sharptooth. Use the capital's Cataclysm portal and move to a fishable pool away from the Temple's dry floor. Keep fishing until each of these THREE checks off.\n\n7. OTHER CATACLYSM ZONES: fish inland Uldum water for Blackbelly Mudfish, Mount Hyjal lakes for Mountain Trout and Striped Lurker, and Twilight Highlands rivers/lakes for Highland Guppy. These are freshwater stops; casting in the coast's sea table instead gives different species. Use Zidormi's earlier Uldum if needed.\n\n8. OUTLAND ZANGARMARSH: fish open lake water for Barbed Gill Trout, Spotted Feltail and Zangarian Sporefish. OUTLAND NAGRAND: fish its lakes for Figluster's Mudfish and Icefin Bluefish. Do not travel to the Draenor zones with the same names.\n\n9. OUTLAND TEROKKAR: fish ordinary rivers for Golden Darter. Fly up to the elevated lakes around Skettis and search for HIGHLAND MIXED SCHOOLS. Fish those schools for Furious Crawdad, Huge Spotted Feltail and the much rarer Goldenscale Vendorfish. Move to the next school when one empties and keep circling the elevated lakes; nearby lowland water does not replace that school route.\n\n10. OUTLAND SHADOWMOON VALLEY: fish GREEN FEL water around 55.8,43.0 for Felblood Snapper. Do not use Draenor Shadowmoon Valley or an ordinary clear-water lake merely because it lies in a zone with the same name. The ordinary Felblood Snapper is required, not the fishing daily's Monstrous Felblood Snapper.\n\n11. NORTHREND WEST: fish Sholazar Basin's inland waters for Barrelhead Goby. Fish Wintergrasp's inland water for Glacial Salmon, Musselback Sculpin, Nettlefish and Giant Darkwater Clam. Loot the clam when caught; it is a different item from The Oceanographer's Darkwater Clam and Abyssal Clam.\n\n12. NORTHREND CENTRAL/EAST: fish Crystalsong Forest's open water for Bonescale Snapper and Glassfin Minnow; Dragonblight's Dragonfin Angelfish Schools for Dragonfin Angelfish; and Howling Fjord's inland water for Fangtooth Herring. Fishing school catches can reduce unwanted species, but do not stop until each named criterion records.\n\n13. NORTHREND DALARAN: fish the Eventide fountain near the south bank for Fountain Goldfish. Move to the OUTDOOR pond in front of Violet Hold for Shimmering Minnow and Slippery Eel, then go down to the Underbelly and fish its sewer water for Sewer Carp. These use different water tables in the same city; use Northrend Dalaran, not Broken Isles Dalaran.\n\n14. Recheck all FORTY-TWO criteria and revisit only missing species. Old lists include Bloated Smallfish/Catfish/Mudsnapper/Redgill/Trout and Plated Armorfish; those are NOT on the current checklist. Goldenscale Vendorfish and Huge Spotted Feltail can take repeated school circuits, so finish common travel catches while waiting for more schools.",
        stepCount = 14,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 37, x = 0.39899999999999997, y = 0.6409999999999999, step = 2, label = "Elwynn - inland lake fishing" },
