    [5479] = {
        achievementId = 5479,
        name = "The Oceanographer",
        category = "Professions",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "The Oceanographer",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Thirty-one catches/drops, with rare fish and two seasonal species.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Thirty-one catches/drops, with rare fish and two seasonal species.\n\n1. Learn Fishing and track the CURRENT thirty-one criteria. Personally catch and loot the fish; Auction House purchases do not award catch credit. Abyssal Clam is the notable DROP exception described below. Do not spend time on removed Bloated-fish criteria.\n\n2. DARKSHORE: use Zidormi's earlier phase when necessary, then fish coastal water for Darkshore Grouper and Slitherskin Mackerel. WETLANDS: fish the coast around Menethil for Firefin Snapper, Oily Blackmouth and Rainbow Fin Albacore. Pool-specific casts and open-water casts have different loot tables.\n\n3. THE HINTERLANDS / EASTERN PLAGUELANDS: fish Hinterlands sea water for Rockscale Cod, then the Eastern Plaguelands COAST for Glossy Mightfish and Spotted Yellowtail. For Redgill, use INLAND water instead; replies recommend Moonglade's Lake Elune'ara when EPL coastal casts do not produce it.\n\n4. SWAMP OF SORROWS: fish the eastern coast for Big-Mouth Clam, Darkclaw Lobster and Large Raw Mightfish. Target Stonescale Eel Swarms when present for Stonescale Eel; otherwise keep fishing appropriate coastal open water. Night fishing can help several rarer species, but a missing single cast is not a broken criterion.\n\n5. SEASONAL CATCHES: catch Summer Bass during its warmer-month fishing season and Winter Squid during its cooler-month season, using the Swamp of Sorrows coast. BOTH remain on the current checklist. If one is out of season, finish the other routes and return in its season; buying it does not replace catching it. Old comments claiming Winter Squid was removed are not the current criteria.\n\n6. BLASTED LANDS: speak to Zidormi near the northern entrance for the earlier landscape, then fish the Tainted Forest's INLAND water for Whitescale Salmon and Sunscale Salmon. Prefer daytime for Sunscale; it is time-sensitive, so do not exhaust a whole night trying to force its daytime catch table.\n\n7. ORIGINAL ISLE OF QUEL'DANAS: use the legacy island, not Midnight's newly rebuilt zone, and fish its coast for Giant Sunfish and Jaggal Clam. For legacy access, speak to Zidormi at Thalassian Pass in Eastern Plaguelands (53.8,8.7) and select the earlier Quel'Thalas. Travel to the original Isle of Quel'Danas and check its old island map before casting.\n\n8. CATACLYSM COASTS: fish the Twilight Highlands sea for Algaefin Rockfish, earlier Uldum sea water for Deepsea Sagefish, and Vashj'ir open water for Fathom Eel and Murglesnout. Moving from an inland river to the sea changes the available fish even within the same zone.\n\n9. ABYSSAL CLAM: in Kelp'thar Forest, kill and LOOT Zin'jatar Raiders around the starting-area naga camps until an Abyssal Clam drops. Check the achievement when looting it, then open it if desired. This criterion is not filled by fishing a Darkwater Clam, and replies about a universal fishing toy do not replace the naga-drop route.\n\n10. NORTHREND BOREAN TUNDRA: fish coastal water for Borean Man O' War, Darkwater Clam and Imperial Manta Ray. Make sure the clam actually enters your bags; do not confuse it with Giant Darkwater Clam from the freshwater achievement.\n\n11. THE FROZEN SEA: move offshore into the open Frozen Sea south of Northrend and fish for Deep Sea Monsterbelly, Moonglow Cuttlefish and Rockfin Grouper. If you only receive a zone's inland fish, move farther out to the sea table while retaining a safe place to cast.\n\n12. HOWLING FJORD: fish coastal or inland water until a Pygmy Suckerfish is looted alongside another catch. It is a companion catch rather than a fish that necessarily replaces your ordinary catch. Recheck all THIRTY-ONE criteria, especially both seasonal fish and the three distinct clams, before declaring the route complete.",
        stepCount = 12,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 62, x = 0.488, y = 0.244, step = 2, label = "Zidormi - earlier Darkshore" },
