        name = "Tol Barad Saboteur",
        category = "PvP",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Tol Barad Saboteur",
        difficulty = "hard",
        difficultyReason = "Twenty deployed enemy siege engines over repeated battles.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Twenty deployed enemy siege engines over repeated battles.\n\n1. Take the capital's Tol Barad portal to the PENINSULA, then cross to the southern battle island. Check the actual zone battle state and join the outdoor Tol Barad battle when it opens. The island and the daily-quest Peninsula are different maps.\n\n2. Use the faction DEFENDING Tol Barad. Find an attacking player's siege engine that has used Deploy Siege Engine and is autonomously firing at a tower. A parked vehicle with its protective rust effect is not the dependable deployed target for Saboteur.\n\n3. Destroy the engine BEFORE it destroys the tower, then find another. Repeat until TWENTY deployed engines are credited across eligible battles. Modern replies report ONE counter point per engine; do not depend on an old double-credit trick.\n\n4. This depends on enemy siege use, so an otherwise empty battle can need another willing participant on the attacking side to earn Veteran and operate engines. Check the counter after the first destruction. A recent Towers of Power comment reports high-level destruction of parked engines can work for that broader criterion; do not assume it satisfies Saboteur's explicit DEPLOYED requirement.",
