    [5501] = {
        achievementId = 5501,
        name = "Fading into Twilight",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Fading into Twilight",
        faction = "Horde",
        difficulty = "medium",
        difficultyReason = "Complete several connected quest chapters, including their prerequisite hand-ins.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete several connected quest chapters, including their prerequisite hand-ins.\n\n1. Enable Trivial Quests on the minimap and track this achievement's CURRENT named chapters. Old comments' numeric quest totals predate storyline tracking. Turn in each branch's final quest and take its follow-up before leaving the hub. Begin the current Machines of War / Twilight Highlands introduction with Eitrigg in Grommash Hold, Orgrimmar. Follow the air-force/naval preparation and the Dragonmaw arrival instead of waiting for the old Garrosh version.\n\n2. Secure Dragonmaw Port with Zaela, then follow BOTH northern and southern flank orders. Continue the Krazzworks and Narkrall the Drake-Tamer route into Bloodgulch. If the trail ends at the Krazzworks, check Gralok around 70,43 for the Narkrall lead.\n\n3. Complete Bloodgulch's Wildhammer conflict through Fury Unbound and its follow-ups. Pick up Garona's A Vision of Twilight branch as well as Mallia's Paint it Black / Earthen Ring lead; these are different story criteria.\n\n4. Follow the northern Earthen Ring story through Torn Ground, Iso'rath's nightmares and the rescue from the Maw of Madness. Continue the Vermillion Redoubt defense, Calen's quests and the Dragon Queen's scripted confrontation. Hand in between events instead of simply waiting at their later locations.\n\n5. Continue the southern assault from your faction's base toward the Twilight Gate. Finish the chapters still unchecked in THIS faction's achievement. The subsequent Initiate Goldmine / Skullcrusher finale awards King of the Mountain and may remain after Fading into Twilight completes.",
        stepCount = 5,
